---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Research Methodology"
  description="How Portuguese Estate researches Portugal property data — INE, AT and AICCOPN sources, limitations, and our partner referral policy."
>
  <section class="site-container py-12 md:py-16 max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="mb-6">Methodology</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Our guides combine publicly available regulatory sources (Diário da República, Autoridade Tributária, IMPIC and AIMA visa rules),
        market reports, and cross-checks against multiple listing platforms. Figures are rounded and dated, and markets move quickly.
      </p>
      <h2>Sources we prioritise</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Official Portuguese sources — INE, Autoridade Tributária, AICCOPN and Diário da República</li>
        <li>Licensed broker market commentary (clearly labelled as third-party)</li>
        <li>Fee schedules published by the Registo Predial, notaries and Autoridade Tributária</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Lead referral policy</h2>
      <p>
        When you submit the shortlist form, your enquiry may be shared with a partner holding an <strong>AMI licence from IMPIC</strong>
        who can show regulated inventory and complete KYC. We do not sell your data to unrelated marketing lists.
      </p>
      <h2>Updates</h2>
      <p>
        Each guide shows an <em>Updated</em> date when material facts change (visa thresholds, fee changes, major market shifts).
        Always confirm numbers with your lawyer and broker before signing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
